Reference data were pulled from Wei et al. (2024), Nature NUMT paper.

1) Download Reference NUMTs:
  a) Reference Numts data comes from: https://github.com/mills-lab/dinumt/blob/master/refNumts.38.bed 
    wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mills-lab/dinumt/master/refNumts.38.bed
  b) Apply 50 bp buffer
    wget https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/hg38/bigZips/hg38.chrom.sizes *expand/buffer each NUMT by 50 bp (to account for small coordinate mismatches)
    bedtools slop -i refNumts.38.bed -g hg38.genome -b 50 > refNumts.38.50bp.bed 

2) Download Non-reference Germline NUMTs: 
    https://github.com/mills-lab/numts-and-aging-in-fibroblasts-and-brains/tree/main/callset/Numt
  a) wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mills-lab/numts-and-aging-in-fibroblasts-and-brains/main/callset/Numt/Numt.1000G.20221202.tar.gz
  b) tar -xzvf Numt.1000G.20221202.tar.gz
  - Using: Numt.1000G/ALL.dinumt.NumtS.1000G.HC.20200604.gt.vcf.gz * Numt.1000G/ directory

3) Filter Your Data:
  #Remove anything overlapping with reference NUMTs.
    # Convert the numts calls txt file Palmer outputs to a bed format
    awk 'NR>1 {print $2"\t"$3"\t"$5"\t"$1"\t"$12"\t"$15}' Output_chr1_numts_calls.txt > chr1_numts.bed

    #Sort the bed frames
    sort -k1,1 -k2,2n chr1_numts.bed > chr1_numts.sorted.bed
    sort -k1,1 -k2,2n refNumts.38.50.bed > refNumts.sorted.bed

    #bedtools subtract [OPTIONS] -a <BED/GFF/VCF> -b <BED/GFF/VCF>
    bedtools intersect -v -a chr2_numts.sorted.bed -b refNumts.sorted.bed > numts_nonoverlap.bed
     * -v = give me entries in A that have no overlap with B 
     * -a your NUMTs
     * -b reference NUMTs

  #Remove anything matching the published germline NUMTs.
  The remaining calls are candidate somatic NUMTs.

